<title>UK: World Bank sets 50 bln lire fungible bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank sets 50 bln lire fungible bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following fungible structured bond was announced by joint lead managers Banca di Roma and Morgan Stanley.</p>
<p>BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p>AMT   **50 BLN LIRE  COUPON    *9.50	MATURITY   *27.MAR.07</p>
<p>TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  98.125    PAY DATE    30.JUN.97</p>
<p>FULL FEES  2.00	LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ   *ANNUAL</p>
<p>MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p>NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p>NOTES     *CALL AT PAR THREE YEARS AFTER WHICH NOTES PAY</p>
<p>		19.50 MINUS TWO TIMES SIX-MONTH LIBOR.</p>
<p>	    **FUNGIBLE WITH EXISTING 600 BLN LIRE DEAL</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
